# Source spreadsheets are working input, not a deliverable: this repository carries numeric
# tables with their source noted, never a copy of the material they came from.
/data/

# Written by the first real import; runtime output, not source.
/store/

# Written by hatchling when the distribution is built. The entry comes before the directory
# can exist: the IDE stages new files by itself, so a build tree would arrive already in the
# index — the same trap /data/ was written for.
/build/

# /data/, /store/ and /build/ carry a leading slash on purpose. Unanchored, each would match a
# directory of that name at any depth, so a fixture tree under tests/ would disappear from the
# repository without anyone being told — the worst way for a fixture to go missing.

# Written per step for the owner to read and run; never part of the history.
commit-plan.ps1